{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update12.json\",\"summary\":\"Added the measured availability consequence of the replay hang for question 29e4214f5ee146b393957fa23a33a73d-question-0: a new source src_leader_stepdown_inflight (raft.go:508-528, how a stepping-down leader fails its inflight logFutures) and a fixed experiment in draft/assurance_multi_test.go (TestAssuranceReplayBlockedMemberAvailability) that builds a three-voter group at MaxAppendEntries 16 with ~3000 committed entries above an absent snapshot, moves leadership away from A, restarts A with a fresh transport in a goroutine with and without RestoreCommittedLogs, waits 8000ms for NewRaft, commits one command with two members live, stops the member that is neither the leader nor A, and commits again. Two comparisons: with the replay on, where the member did not return from NewRaft, the surviving pair must still commit; the flag-off control must also commit. Local construction feedback showed exactly the intended difference (replay on: A blocked with restoreFromCommittedLogs in the stack, commit with two live, then 'leadership lost while committing log' after the second stop; replay off: NewRaft returned, and the surviving pair committed), and the retained receipt is requested. Comparison count dropped from three to two because a result event cannot also establish its own admission.\"}"}}
